&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Flexport:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flexport, we believe global trade can move the human race forward. That’s why it’s our mission to make global commerce so easy there will be more of it. We’re shaping the future of a $10T industry with solutions powered by innovative technology and exceptional people. Today, companies of all sizes—from emerging brands to Fortune 500s—use Flexport technology to move more than $19B of merchandise across 112 countries a year.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The recent global supply chain crisis has put Flexport center stage as we continue to play a pivotal role in how goods move around the world. We are proud to have the support of the best investors in the game who believe in our mission, solutions and people. Ready to tackle global challenges that impact business, society, and the environment? Come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To continue our global expansion, we&#39;re looking for a Trucking Pricing Associate to work within our trucking organization. We are looking for an individual who is detail-oriented, analytically driven, and comfortable operating in a fast-paced environment where accuracy and speed directly impact revenue. In this role you will manage pricing requests, bids, and formal RFPs across Drayage, Cartage/LTL, FTL, and Transload - synthesizing market data, collaborating with procurement on carrier negotiations, and delivering competitive rates that protect margin and win business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with demand and partner pricing teams to support the acquisition of strategic accounts through comprehensive pricing exercises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strategies to win trucking business for our freight forwarding client base&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage RFPs for trucking and coordinate with regional trucking procurement team to ensure we have the service offerings in place to win the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide account executives with the necessary trucking network intelligence to secure new business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up, implement and drive new procurement strategies and programs that will enable Flexport to build a more competitive trucking product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct complex network studies based on volume flows, strategic priorities and market trends to develop recommendations on future trucking procurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide insights and visibility to the regional procurement teams to enable them to make data driven decisions in regards to procurement strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable the global trucking team to accurately report on cost and net revenue for all trucking services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You should have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Supply Chain, Industrial Engineering, BBA or similar relevant area of study is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years of prior experience as a Supply Chain Solutions Analyst or in Supply Chain or Management Consulting, Investment Banking, Private Equity or Venture Capital Research would be preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in building complex data models on Excel, developing macros and prior SQL knowledge is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in market research, building reporting tools and dashboards and working on process improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in the Logistics industry or developing strategy for ground transportation would be a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinking and ground floor execution - no job is too big or too small&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional technical aptitude and strong desire for learning new technologies and solution architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &quot;compliance first&quot; attitude to keep our regulators happy and enthusiastic about Flexport since we operate in a heavily regulated industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
